<PageLayout title="Darwin's Monsters" kicker='PROJECT // CONCEPT BUILD' lead='Every species is strange if you look closely enough.'>
<section><div class="prose content-page"><p>Darwin's Monsters is a science-communication project about the extraordinary forms evolution has produced: biological solutions that appear monstrous, elegant, absurd or impossible until their evolutionary context is understood.</p><p>The project is designed to connect a podcast identity with interactive web stories. It is intentionally broad: extinct and living species, microorganisms and animals, fossils and genomes, familiar organisms and obscure lineages can all become entries.</p><h2>$ principle</h2><p>The goal is not to build a cabinet of evolutionary “freaks.” It is to use unusual organisms as doors into real biology: constraint, convergence, trade-offs, developmental history, ecology and contingency.</p><h2>$ formats</h2><ul><li>Short species stories</li><li>Interactive phylogenetic context</li><li>Genomic and evolutionary side notes</li><li>Podcast episodes and companion visual material</li><li>Collections organized by evolutionary problems rather than taxonomic popularity</li></ul></div></section>
</PageLayout>